<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom starts buyback programme.</title>
<headline>Telecom starts buyback programme.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom Corp of New Zealand said it had bought back 500,000 of its shares at NZ$6.85 each on Thursday in the first purchase of a NZ$1 billion buyback programme.  </p>
<p>Telecom said Thursday's purchase represented 0.026 percent of the shares on issue.</p>
<p>The shares closed at $6.85, down two cents.</p>
<p>Telecom said last November it planned a NZ$1 billion share repurchase programme over one year starting in the fourth quarter of its 1996/97 fiscal year. Half the shares would be purchased on the New Zealand and New York stock exchanges and the other half directly from Ameritech and Bell Atlantic, which each own a quarter of the company.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
